      "create_requirement": {
        "description": "\nPropose a new Requirement (e.g. an HLR or LLR) via the MCP import path.\n\nThis creates a PROPOSAL, not a final record. Every requirement submitted\nthrough this tool is tagged status=\"proposed\" and provenance=\"mcp\" \u2014\nhardcoded below, not caller-controlled, so a model can't self-approve by\npassing a different status. Per the 2026-07-12 team meeting, MCP is a\nthird way work enters PACT, alongside manual entry and smart import, each\ngated by the same downstream flow: a human pre-review, then PACT's own\nformal peer review and compliance tracking before anything counts as\naccepted. No tool in this file can move a requirement out of \"proposed\" \u2014\nthat transition is a human action inside PACT's own UI, the same\nrestriction sign_review (below) already applies to review sign-off.\n\nlevel: e.g. \"System\", \"High-Level\", \"Low-Level\".\nparent_id: the parent Requirement this one traces up to, if any.\nagent_name: which AI tool is submitting this (e.g. \"claude\", \"codex\",\n    \"copilot\", \"gemini\") \u2014 multiple AI tools will submit through this\n    same door, so provenance needs to record which one, not just \"mcp\".\n",
